  "spec_section": "protocol.md §9.5.2 (paired_extensions canonical JSON inside vault.prefs)",
  "description": "Pins protocol::paired_extension::parse_paired_extensions_array — the canonical-JSON decoder for the paired_extensions array embedded in vault.prefs (browser-clipper pairing registry, MYND-329 family). parse_ok cases pin the decoded record-set as its canonical re-encoding (NFC folding + lexicographic key order + (extension_id, token_value)-sort; the additive optional paired_at is emitted only when present) plus the exact consumed byte count; parse_fail cases pin the closed error surface (malformed / missing_field / wrong_type). The bearer token_value is serde-skipped on the IPC boundary but written explicitly by the on-disk codec, so it round-trips here. Cases generated by `cargo test -p protocol --lib emit_paired_extension_vectors_for_paste -- --ignored`.",
